httpjet (0.2.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Security: validate the upstream WebSocket handshake; strip credentials and
    keep non-ASCII cookie lines in capsule revalidation; decode every gzip
    member of a backend response; fail an LSAPI response whose stream packet
    precedes its header; escape control characters in the text error log;
    refuse an LSAPI socket path another live process serves.
  * QUIC: drop connections lost before their handshake and keep their slot
    counted; send Drained exactly once; charge shared cache bodies to the
    connection only.
  * Startup: build the rewrite prefilter off the request path, parse each
    .htaccess once and before serving, and reuse parsed files across reloads.
  * Steer listeners by CPU only when the NIC's receive fan-out reaches every
    worker; count HTTP/2 connection ends and page-cache ghost hits.
  * Packaging: fix the lsphp reload unit, readiness-marker reads, TLS pair
    validation and the installer tests.

 -- Mike Fara <35661811+faratech@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

httpjet (0.1.12-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Reduce hot-path allocation and contention: borrowed vhost routing,
    a single-pass fast-serve header scan, HPACK header-name reuse, and
    sharded telemetry and bridge counters.
  * Refine the page-cache disk store and metadata blob handling, the
    fast-memo and page-memo serve paths, and access-log rendering.

 -- Mike Fara <35661811+faratech@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

httpjet (0.1.11-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Default the io_uring transport to cooperative task running
    (--uring-ring coop) and enable the page-cache response memo for cookieless
    public hits (--no-page-cache-response-memo disables it).
  * Steer accepted connections to the CPU that received them (SO_INCOMING_CPU;
    --no-cpu-steering disables it), reuse HTTP/1.1 write buffers, reuse the
    encoded HPACK Date literal and format access-log lines without core::fmt.
  * Schedule HTTP/3 streams fairly and add opt-in HTTP/3 send experiments:
    --h3-engine, --h3-send-batch and --h3-gso-segments.

 -- Mike Fara <35661811+faratech@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

